    "chunk_text": "Sustained economic growth cannot rely indefinitely on externally driven reform agendas. State institutions and administrative systems must develop the ability to identify weaknesses, implement corrective measures, and maintain reform momentum without constant dependence on external partners\n\nFor Sri Lanka, this raises a practical challenge. Sustained economic growth cannot rely indefinitely on externally driven reform agendas. State institutions and administrative systems must develop the ability to identify weaknesses, implement corrective measures, and maintain reform momentum without constant dependence on external partners. The country is currently on its 17th IMF program since independence. This alone suggests that if government institutions had been able to convert external support into lasting stability, repeated recourse to the Fund would not have been necessary."
